' Causal paths of one plan under the legacy and the compacted splitter
' (DR-84, cap root cause C9). An operation of participant P at step s has the
' path P (s, 0). The legacy splitter gives child i of a split at step s the
' participant path P (s, 1) (i, 0); the compacted splitter gives it P (s, i + 1).
' Both renderings sort the operation paths of the plan in the same order, so
' the scheduler fires the same COMMs in the same order.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-decision-records.md (DR-84);
'                  rholang/src/rust/interpreter/deterministic_reduction.rs
'                  (ReductionContext::split, next_operation).
' Formal model:    formal/rocq/cost_accounted_rho/theories/DetachedPathCompaction.v
'                  (render_order_isomorphism, fuse_injective,
'                  fuse_halves_participant_depth, naive_fusion_collides).
' Palette:  plan = control amber · legacy paths = supply blue
'           compacted paths = pool green · naive fusion = red
'           order result = note green
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/detached-path-compaction.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh detached-path-compaction.puml)

@startuml detached-path-compaction
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #333333
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor $ca_neutral
title Causal paths of one plan under the two splitters (DR-84)

rectangle "**plan of the root participant**\nstep 0: operation\nstep 1: split into child 0 and child 1\n    child 0, its step 0: operation\n    child 1, its step 0: split into one grandchild\n        grandchild, its step 0: operation\nstep 2: operation (after the children rejoin)" as Plan $ca_control

rectangle "**legacy operation paths, sorted**\n1. (0,0)\n2. (1,1) (0,0) (0,0)\n3. (1,1) (1,0) (0,1) (0,0) (0,0)\n4. (2,0)\nlongest path: 5 segments" as Legacy $ca_supply

rectangle "**compacted operation paths, sorted**\n1. (0,0)\n2. (1,1) (0,0)\n3. (1,2) (0,1) (0,0)\n4. (2,0)\nlongest path: 3 segments" as Compact $ca_pool

rectangle "**naive fusion (s, i)**\nOp 1 gives (1,0)\nChild 1 0 also gives (1,0)\n(naive_fusion_collides)" as Naive $ca_rejectfill

rectangle "**same rank for every operation**\n<latex>\mathrm{cmp}(\mathrm{compact}(u), \mathrm{compact}(v)) = \mathrm{cmp}(\mathrm{legacy}(u), \mathrm{legacy}(v))</latex>\n(render_order_isomorphism)\nk nested splits: <latex>k + 1</latex> segments instead of <latex>2k + 1</latex>" as Same $ca_note_green

Plan --> Legacy : legacy splitter\nchild i = (s,1) (i,0)
Plan --> Compact : compacted splitter\nchild i = (s, i + 1)
Plan -[$ca_debit]-> Naive : rejected fusion\nchild i = (s, i)
Legacy --> Same
Compact --> Same

note bottom of Naive $ca_note_grey
  A participant uses one step counter for its
  operations and its splits, so the program never
  makes this pair. The chosen fusion keeps the
  order without that invariant: (s, i + 1) > (s, 0).
end note

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_control>| one participant plan (the units of the paths) |
  |<$ca_supply>| paths of the legacy splitter |
  |<$ca_pool>| paths of the compacted splitter (C9) |
  |<$ca_rejectfill>| fusion that is not injective (negative control) |
  |<$ca_note_green>| the order result that keeps schedules unchanged |
endlegend

@enduml
